gned}\\sqrt{6} & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41977/selection/e529487144d1b9c31adbc43bc3fccba03ba51f20dbfc82eb6441bf4181ba12ff" :answer/id #uuid "e5d7c919-f82d-5fee-90cc-a893fb7be0d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{5} & -3.2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41977/selection/4e7cea7fa43f8053990c9ae64ff656bdda3a84d88cd01fc2f73c469c50ea04c2" :answer/id #uuid "5c61e51f-fb32-5b4e-8a47-1a09f71f27e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41977/selection/fe9715ce6bcb9d06bdccf76d6b6db33a9b49b11d7179b2362ab3285b4e84ee9f" :answer/id #uuid "668fab7c-53a5-52b6-a4fc-a8d0cf36605f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41977/selection/c0d28c72c11b30d78ace58aa16f3eb0d07968cdcf8a6185b50ba62857f4711b6" :answer/id #uuid "6a89f43d-9e54-58cb-b803-f19488322895" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{7} \\\\ -3.2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41977/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c3793e72-05ae-547f-b526-5db132a90f0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-41977/selection/e529487144d1b9c31adbc43bc3fccba03ba51f20dbfc82eb6441bf4181ba12ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-41977/selection/a0c34394fcb1a3829ba0e32ffdfa0dc6f2fc0d9b5e92d66d25bb427f3a637ea2" "q-41977/selection/e529487144d1b9c31adbc43bc3fccba03ba51f20dbfc82eb6441bf4181ba12ff" "q-41977/selection/4e7cea7fa43f8053990c9ae64ff656bdda3a84d88cd01fc2f73c469c50ea04c2" "q-41977/selection/fe9715ce6bcb9d06bdccf76d6b6db33a9b49b11d7179b2362ab3285b4e84ee9f" "q-41977/selection/c0d28c72c11b30d78ace58aa16f3eb0d07968cdcf8a6185b50ba62857f4711b6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-41977" :question/id #uuid "ebc5630e-e6db-53b3-a857-6c1c02e997fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-41977" :question/problem "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\sqrt{7} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{5} & -3.2 \\\\ \\sqrt{6} & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $B$ by the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}$ on the *left*, the result must be the $2$nd *row* of $B.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{5} & -3.2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\sqrt{7} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{5} & -3.2 \\\\ \\sqrt{6} & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{5} & -3.2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-41977/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89362140-1a17-56fd-a9ab-4da336112bee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-41977"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4408"] :question/problem "Calculate the product $I_3 B$ given that $I_3$ is the $3 \\times 3$ identity matrix and\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/assets/9b8d8f439845a4949789fe313997d2245249e1a4df58c750d7cda0af36f1ce18.png)" :question/worked-solution "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $I_3$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/assets/ac591cf90fae6e8275fed52c26c8487bff9d654733d414974631948fe30b8150.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4410"] :question/problem "Calculate the product $C D,$ if\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/assets/945664c408577aac1d1a745120b3c17c46fd9db93e6d26cc53a4e501390936e2.png)\nand \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/assets/907ffa0b29d96249fe03a7fce3fe682c08982b14c7b7f72840540e6269196425.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $D$ is the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix $I_3.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $C$ by the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix $I_3,$ the result must be the $2$nd *column* of $C.$ Therefore,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043295/assets/980ae75452824b4a8aa701b4e11be8c31448557933357458329f0a2b73a1cca6.png)\n\nDon't believe it? Let's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0 \\\\ -1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 5\\cdot 0+4\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
